<!--
  p1_draft_esi.xml - DRAFT EtherCAT Slave Information for Platform 1
  (STM32H723 + LAN9252 SPI, SOES, one CiA402 axis), GD9 step 9.4.

  Purpose: let TwinCAT build the MIXED ENI (eni_mixed.xml: Box 1 = this
  slave, Box 2 = the commercial servo) before the P1 firmware exists. The
  PDO layout is the one agreed in roadmap_platform1_slave.md (Giai doan 5):
    RxPDO 0x1600 (13 byte): 0x6040 Controlword U16, 0x6060 Modes of
      operation S8, 0x607A Target position S32, 0x60FF Target velocity S32,
      0x6071 Target torque S16
    TxPDO 0x1A00 (15 byte): 0x6041 Statusword U16, 0x6061 Modes display S8,
      0x6064 Position actual S32, 0x606C Velocity actual S32, 0x6077 Torque
      actual S16, 0x603F Error code U16
    TxPDO 0x1A01 (6 byte, proposal): 0x2F00:01 SYNC0->RxPDO done, :02
      SYNC0->duty applied, :03 FOC ISR max (us), U16 each
  DC SYNC0 (AssignActivate 0x0300), FreeRun. CoE with SDO Info, PDO assign
  and Complete Access (SOES supports all three).

  DRAFT - NOT for writing a real EEPROM:
    - Vendor 0x00000499 is the project's test placeholder (not ETG-assigned);
      product 0x00000102 / revision 0x00000001 are placeholders. The real
      values come from the slave project; every PDO change must raise the
      revision (SOEM ecx_lookup_mapping reuses the mapping of an identical
      identity - giai_doan_2_tong_hop.md section 5).
    - ConfigData words 0..6 are the soft_bus values (word 0 = 0x0080 PDI
      SPI); they must be re-derived from the LAN9252 datasheet before the
      EEPROM is written (ke_hoach_ethercat_v2.md section 1.2).
    - Sizes of SM2/SM3 below are the PDO sizes; the mailbox is 128 byte like
      soft_bus. Check against the SOES configuration of the firmware.
  Validate with tools/esi/check_xsd.sh config/esi/p1_draft_esi.xml.
-->
